From: OCCTSwift ecosystem <noreply@secondmouse.au>
Subject: [PATCH] Modeling Algorithms - BRepFilletAPI_MakeFillet builds fillets on opposite edges whose arcs cross

Two fillets on the opposite edges of a face with r1 + r2 > w (a 4 mm face, 3 and 3) are
refused by the stripe builder, which has no section curve for stripes that cross (#1177).

When Compute() fails for contours that share no vertex and are all of constant radius, Build
now returns the intersection (BRepAlgoAPI_Common) of the shape filleted on each contour alone:
each arc stays tangent to the face it starts on and the arcs cross on the face between them.
The result must be one valid closed solid that removes at least the largest and at most the
sum of what each contour removes; otherwise the failure stands.

Related to #1568.

The DRAW case bugs moddata_1 bug203 expected the fillet of two edges next to a chamfer to be
refused; the case now checks the shape if it is built.

Upstream: Open-Cascade-SAS/OCCT#1670 (fork branch SecondMouseAU/OCCT fix/fillet-opposite-edges-wide-radii). This is the form of that
pull request as it stacks on the earlier patches of this series; where it differs from the pull request
as submitted it is only in the lines the stack made conflict (see Scripts/patches/README.md). The DRAW
test cases under tests/ that the pull request edits are not part of this patch: the build has no Draw.

---
